From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:26:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: ufs: samsung,exynos-ufs: Add Exynos9820 UFS host

The host controller of this SoC takes the four register windows this
binding already describes and the two clocks that come with them: the
one the controller runs on and the one of the link, whose rate every
timing of that link is computed from.

The bits that decide whether its transfers are coherent sit in the FSYS1
system register block rather than in a window of the controller, so they
are reached through samsung,sysreg, which this binding already carries.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/samsung,exynos-ufs.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/samsung,exynos-ufs.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/samsung,exynos-ufs.yaml
index 710ce493f3b..dfee7f7acf2 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/samsung,exynos-ufs.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/samsung,exynos-ufs.yaml
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@ properties:
     enum:
       - google,gs101-ufs
       - samsung,exynos7-ufs
+      - samsung,exynos9820-ufs
       - samsung,exynosautov9-ufs
       - samsung,exynosautov9-ufs-vh
       - samsung,exynosautov920-ufs
